  "goodToKnow": "Die Mitschuld is a share of the blame or complicity: eine Mitschuld tragen (to bear part of the blame), Mitschuld am Unfall. In insurance and traffic law, it's contributory negligence: a cyclist without lights may have a Mitschuld. Mitschuldig means partly to blame. Die Schuld means guilt or blame, and in plural Schulden, debts. It has no plural."
